; Gamma's sort: two cells out of order exchange their values.  Indices and
; values are the same four names, ordered by the (less A B) rows.  The cells
; hold 3 1 4 2: three inversions, and each shares a cell with another.  Every
; step sorts them but two: every has no step, since its matches take the same
; cells and so are not jointly enabled, and unique sees three matches.
(at one three)
(at two one)
(at three four)
(at four two)
(less one two)
(less one three)
(less one four)
(less two three)
(less two four)
(less three four)
(rule swap (take (at $i $x) (at $j $y)) (read (less $i $j) (less $y $x))
  (make (at $i $y) (at $j $x)))
